    <other_details id="References">Archetypes: openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.care_relationship.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.role_assignment.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PERSON.generic_person.v1. Structure derived from the openEHR CKM demographic drafts (openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PERSON.person.v0, PERSON.person-patient.v0, PARTY_IDENTITY.person_name.v0, ROLE.individual_provider.v0, CAPABILITY.individual_credentials.v0). Names, addresses, telecom and contact persons use the published CKM clusters openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.structured_name.v1, address.v1, electronic_communication.v1 and person.v1. Aligned with the HL7 FHIR R4 (4.0.1) resources Patient, Practitioner and RelatedPerson (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/).</other_details>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>A patient as a party beside the EHR, the party an EHR_STATUS subject references. It names no one: it holds the patient number or a pseudonym, the year of birth, the administrative gender and whether the patient has died, and the patient's relationships to care providers, care teams, organisations and roles.</purpose>
      <keywords>patient</keywords>
      <keywords>pseudonym</keywords>
      <keywords>EHR subject</keywords>
      <keywords>care relationship</keywords>
      <use>Use for the party that stands for a patient in the clinical domain, where who the patient is is kept apart in a PERSON-PatientIdentity.v1 party. The identifier is the patient number or the pseudonym (DV_IDENTIFIER type MR, PI or ANON); the only identity is a pseudonym. A care relationship to a care provider, a care team or an organisation puts the patient in their care; a role assignment gives the patient a shared role.</use>
      <misuse>Not for names, addresses, telecom, a full date of birth or a national person number: the template has no place for them, and they belong in PERSON-PatientIdentity.v1.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openehr-reference-content contributors</copyright>
    </details>
  </description>
